# BMAD: personal config (user-scoped) and per-developer artifacts.
# Note: project-scoped planning-artifacts (PRDs, briefs, ADRs) are committed team artifacts.
# Note: project-scoped implementation-artifacts are gitignored (per-developer scratch).
_bmad/custom/.active-project
_bmad-output/projects/*/implementation-artifacts/
# ...and the same path as a SYMLINK. The trailing-slash rule above matches only
# real directories, so in a bmad-loop home -- where `bmad-loop-worktree` creates
# implementation-artifacts as a Tier-3 backlink to the main checkout -- the path
# comes back untracked, and `bmad-loop run` refuses to start on a dirty worktree.
# No trailing slash = matches the symlink too.
_bmad-output/projects/*/implementation-artifacts

# bmad-loop / upstream-tooling seam: root artifact dirs are LOCAL symlinks to the
# active project's dirs (re-point on `bmad-switch`).
_bmad-output/planning-artifacts
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts
_bmad-output/projects/*/.bmad-config.user.toml

# bmad-loop runtime scratch: run worktrees and their cache, never tracked.
.bmad-loop/runs/
.bmad-loop/cache/
# Derived harness policy: rendered whole from the canonical EffectivePolicy on
# every `marshal config --write-harness-policy` run (AD-12/AD-35). The model
# classifies it generated-derived, so leaving it tracked leaves every adopting
# repo permanently dirty -- the same failure the symlink rule above prevents.
.bmad-loop/policy.toml
# Derived artifact (Story 33.3, SPEC-marshal-token-economy CAP-2): the
# wire-compression bmad-loop profile overlay `factory spin` writes per
# adapter when the `wire` layer is on. Untracked and not ignored, it makes
# `bmad-loop run` refuse the loop home with "git worktree is not clean" --
# the same failure shape `.bmad-loop/policy.toml` above already exists to
# prevent.
.bmad-loop/profiles/

# The plan artifact (AD-57): derived, cheap to regenerate, and a committed
# stale plan is a hazard -- so the plan file is ignored, but NOT the whole
# `.marshal/` directory: `.marshal/seed-state.yml` is git-tracked (AD-52).
.marshal/plan.json
